{"parentUuid":"0372199d-85c4-486e-bc02-ce1bcb8e257e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_015VdnafrbzLDWJaD7CBkuCt","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"additionalContext\":\"<context_guidance>\\n  <tip>\\n    When you intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate), use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries) for multiple commands or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language: \\\"javascript\\\", code: \\\"...\\\") for one — the raw output stays in the sandbox and only what you print enters your conversation. Shell stays the right surface when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation); if you use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language: \\\"shell\\\"), write syntax for the host shell.\\n  </tip>\\n</context_guidance>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/pretooluse.mjs\"","durationMs":158},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5274eac2-3c42-4166-af33-537cb15f7020","timestamp":"2026-09-10T22:32:07.034Z","session_id":"5f2ac916-6e52-43f6-bc78-4e7231c4afa0","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA","sessionId":"5f2ac916-6e52-43f6-bc78-4e7231c4afa0","version":"2.1.268","gitBranch":"main"}
