{"parentUuid":"8dd2bcf0-f3a8-4269-8253-0ea2dcc3ad84","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CevZSJpLMxsofyRBGuhmN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SAiS5d5L3HGYmymWiXVVe5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_dcg-guard-blocks.md; echo \"=== INDEX dcg/settings lines ===\"; grep -in 'dcg\\|settings.json\\|BOM' ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/MEMORY.md","description":"Read existing dcg memory and index lines"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2064,"cache_read_input_tokens":81635,"output_tokens":311,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":111},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2064,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":81635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2064,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2064},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CevZSHqJX3BtXJ7b6ayW8","attributionSkill":"memory-write","type":"assistant","uuid":"a644f18e-4044-4b22-aa70-17a997979a1c","timestamp":"2026-09-10T22:37:52.238Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"5f2ac916-6e52-43f6-bc78-4e7231c4afa0","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA","sessionId":"5f2ac916-6e52-43f6-bc78-4e7231c4afa0","version":"2.1.268","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"a644f18e-4044-4b22-aa70-17a997979a1c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ef54ef8f-de69-4bc6-b0ab-a9e40b82a9fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SAiS5d5L3HGYmymWiXVVe5","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: dcg-guard-blocks\ndescription: \"The dcg command guard blocks whole compound commands — which shapes trip it, and the rewrite that gets the work done\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 80892ff4-3719-4a85-aa22-4eaf3500081d\n  modified: 2026-09-08T02:19:00.806Z\n---\n\nThe `dcg` guard sits in front of Bash and rejects a command **before any of it runs**.\nIt blocks the *whole* invocation, not the offending line — so a `set -e` script with\nfour good steps and one blocked step accomplishes nothing, silently.\n\n**Shapes confirmed to block (2026-09-07):**\n\n- `mv` where either side mentions `~`, `$HOME`, `/etc`, `/usr`, `/var`, `/home`.\n  Rule `core.filesystem:mv-sensitive-source-root-home`. It is guarding the\n  \"relocate then delete\" bypass (`mv /etc /tmp/x && rm -rf /tmp/x`), so it fires\n  on shape alone — an ordinary `mv ~/foo ~/DEV/foo` is caught.\n  **Fix: write both paths absolute** — `mv /Users/kristinarash/foo /Users/kristinarash/DEV/foo`\n  passes. Verified on four real moves.\n- `git branch -d` / `-D` / `-M` / `-C`. Rule `core.git:branch-force-delete`.\n  No rewrite gets past this one — deleting a merged branch needs the user to run it.\n  **Do not bundle it with a push**: a `git push … ; git branch -d …` one-liner is\n  rejected as a unit and the push never happens.\n\n**The habit that follows:** when a multi-step shell job touches home paths or refs,\nrun the steps as separate calls, or at minimum keep any guard-prone step out of the\nsame invocation as work you need to land. Then verify — a blocked command produces\nan error, but a *partially* useful compound produces nothing at all.\n\n`dcg explain \"<command>\"` prints the rule and suggested alternatives.\n\nRelated: [[zsh-shell-traps]], [[keystoneos-verification-habits]]\n=== INDEX dcg/settings lines ===\n46:- [dcg guard blocks](project_dcg-guard-blocks.md) — a Bash command was rejected outright; which shapes trip it and the rewrite that works","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4b5600a6-ad0f-441f-be59-c2579ff05a9f","timestamp":"2026-09-10T22:37:54.255Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: dcg-guard-blocks\ndescription: \"The dcg command guard blocks whole compound commands — which shapes trip it, and the rewrite that gets the work done\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 80892ff4-3719-4a85-aa22-4eaf3500081d\n  modified: 2026-09-08T02:19:00.806Z\n---\n\nThe `dcg` guard sits in front of Bash and rejects a command **before any of it runs**.\nIt blocks the *whole* invocation, not the offending line — so a `set -e` script with\nfour good steps and one blocked step accomplishes nothing, silently.\n\n**Shapes confirmed to block (2026-09-07):**\n\n- `mv` where either side mentions `~`, `$HOME`, `/etc`, `/usr`, `/var`, `/home`.\n  Rule `core.filesystem:mv-sensitive-source-root-home`. It is guarding the\n  \"relocate then delete\" bypass (`mv /etc /tmp/x && rm -rf /tmp/x`), so it fires\n  on shape alone — an ordinary `mv ~/foo ~/DEV/foo` is caught.\n  **Fix: write both paths absolute** — `mv /Users/kristinarash/foo /Users/kristinarash/DEV/foo`\n  passes. Verified on four real moves.\n- `git branch -d` / `-D` / `-M` / `-C`. Rule `core.git:branch-force-delete`.\n  No rewrite gets past this one — deleting a merged branch needs the user to run it.\n  **Do not bundle it with a push**: a `git push … ; git branch -d …` one-liner is\n  rejected as a unit and the push never happens.\n\n**The habit that follows:** when a multi-step shell job touches home paths or refs,\nrun the steps as separate calls, or at minimum keep any guard-prone step out of the\nsame invocation as work you need to land. Then verify — a blocked command produces\nan error, but a *partially* useful compound produces nothing at all.\n\n`dcg explain \"<command>\"` prints the rule and suggested alternatives.\n\nRelated: [[zsh-shell-traps]], [[keystoneos-verification-habits]]\n=== INDEX dcg/settings lines ===\n46:- [dcg guard blocks](project_dcg-guard-blocks.md) — a Bash command was rejected outright; which shapes trip it and the rewrite that works","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a644f18e-4044-4b22-aa70-17a997979a1c","session_id":"5f2ac916-6e52-43f6-bc78-4e7231c4afa0","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA","sessionId":"5f2ac916-6e52-43f6-bc78-4e7231c4afa0","version":"2.1.268","gitBranch":"main"}
